.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1957</span><span class="rf-text">On 1 January the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saarland">Saarland</a> joins <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1990</span><span class="rf-text">On 3 October after the Two Plus Four Treaty, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-germany">German Democratic Republic</a> is dissolved and its five re-established states accede to the Federal Republic.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1991</span><span class="rf-text">On 15 March <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> regains its full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">2002</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> introduces the euro; the European Central Bank sits in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">2005</span><span class="rf-text">Angela Merkel becomes the first female chancellor.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">2022</span><span class="rf-text">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, Chancellor Olaf Scholz announces a one-time 100 billion euro infusion into the Bundeswehr and spending beyond <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>'s 2% target.</span></li></ol>
